From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: keep UBWC on MUTABLE_FORMAT images

Adapted from:
https://github.com/Vauzi-17/710/blob/6828465a8bc2ae08b705e4a67a6a2bb76197e231/patches/30-tu-z-mutable.py

On GPUs without ubwc_all_formats_compatible (A722 included), upstream drops
UBWC for MUTABLE_FORMAT images. TU_Z_MUTABLE picks the behavior:
  0, 1  upstream (UBWC off)
  2     UBWC kept (default)
Images whose format list has component swaps, or that have no format list,
still fall back to linear as upstream: tiled views can't swap components, so
a BGRA view of RGBA texels would swap red and blue. The Turnip-Z original
kept those tiled too. R8G8<->R16 reinterpretation also stays linear.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
index 8d8c7ae..b3ba154 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 #include "tu_subsampled_image.h"
 #include "tu_wsi.h"

+DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(tu_z_mutable, "TU_Z_MUTABLE", 2)
+
 uint32_t
 tu6_plane_count(VkFormat format)
 {
@@ -628,7 +630,8 @@ tu_image_init(struct tu_device *device, struct tu_image *image,
             ubwc_enabled = false;
             force_linear_tile = true;
          } else if (!mutable_ubwc_fc) {
-            if (ubwc_enabled) {
+            int64_t z_mutable = debug_get_option_tu_z_mutable();
+            if (ubwc_enabled && z_mutable < 2) {
                if (fmt_list && fmt_list->viewFormatCount == 2) {
                   perf_debug(
                      device,
